.TH SDL_SINT64_C 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SINT64_C \- Append the 64 bit integer suffix to a signed integer literal.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_SINT64_C(c)  c ## LL  /* or whatever the current compiler uses. */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This helps compilers that might believe a integer literal larger than 0xFFFFFFFF is overflowing a 32-bit value\[char46] Use
.BR SDL_SINT64_C(0xFFFFFFFF1)
instead of
.BR 0xFFFFFFFF1
by itself\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

